WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.045 --> 00:00:14.429
"No!" Zann yelled.

2
00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:15.669
But it was too late.

3
00:00:16.489 --> 00:00:18.870
Darb, Gliss, and Zing were gone.

4
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.011
"I couldn't hold on!"

5
00:00:21.231 --> 00:00:21.812
Perda cried.

6
00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:24.713
"I tried to hold on to Gliss, but I couldn't!"

7
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:27.014
"I know," Zann said.

8
00:00:27.874 --> 00:00:30.035
He was glad Perda had restored the Shackle spell.

9
00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:32.616
Otherwise, his friends might all be gone.

10
00:00:33.748 --> 00:00:35.469
"We have to get out of the vortex.

11
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.511
Then we'll figure out what to do."

12
00:00:38.492 --> 00:00:39.292
He glanced around.

13
00:00:39.732 --> 00:00:43.355
A wormhole was sliding past, showing a peaceful green meadow.

14
00:00:44.636 --> 00:00:47.258
He lunged for it, but his hand came up empty.

15
00:00:48.159 --> 00:00:49.500
"How do we get through one?"

16
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.320
Perda asked.

17
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.921
"I don't know."

18
00:00:52.662 --> 00:00:55.204
Zann grabbed for another wormhole and missed again.

19
00:00:55.224 --> 00:00:58.286
"Wyssa got me out the first time.

20
00:00:58.886 --> 00:01:00.888
And Zing brought us out into Skellia."

21
00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:04.657
He felt a pang of despair as he said Zing's name.

22
00:01:05.558 --> 00:01:07.958
Would he ever see his fiery little buddy again?

23
00:01:08.739 --> 00:01:09.979
Or Darb, his best friend?

24
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.421
Or Gliss, whom he'd accidentally dragged into danger yet again?

25
00:01:15.401 --> 00:01:16.782
Zann tried not to think about it.

26
00:01:16.802 --> 00:01:20.764
"Zing got us out when he tried to grab that fish he saw.

27
00:01:21.624 --> 00:01:25.986
He spotted it through the Skellia wormhole and really jumped at it.

28
00:01:26.906 --> 00:01:27.286
Hang on.

29
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:29.687
I'm going to try harder for the next one."

30
00:01:30.768 --> 00:01:35.794
"Okay. But even if that works, how will we know which world we're entering?"

31
00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:36.675
Perda wondered.

32
00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:38.015
"We won't.

33
00:01:38.216 --> 00:01:40.877
But anywhere has got to be better than here, right?"

34
00:01:42.078 --> 00:01:43.218
Zann glanced forward.

35
00:01:43.238 --> 00:01:44.299
"Hold on!"

36
00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:47.481
He hurled himself toward the next wormhole.

37
00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:51.563
This time he felt his fingers latch onto the edge of the wormhole.

38
00:01:52.323 --> 00:01:54.184
Its magic energy burned his hand.

39
00:01:54.204 --> 00:01:57.366
"Ouch!" he cried, letting go.

40
00:01:58.346 --> 00:02:01.048
He caught a glimpse of a gleaming city as he tumbled away.

41
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.482
"Drat!" "What happened?"

42
00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:04.282
Perda asked.

43
00:02:04.943 --> 00:02:07.185
"Nothing. I'll try again in a second."

44
00:02:08.025 --> 00:02:11.508
This time Zann vowed not to let go, no matter what.

45
00:02:12.429 --> 00:02:13.870
He lunged at the next wormhole.

46
00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:19.855
His fingers caught the edge, and he ignored the magical burn, pulling himself forward.

47
00:02:20.856 --> 00:02:26.080
"Oof!" he said as he slid through the wormhole and fell flat on his face on the other

48
00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.422
side. Perda landed beside him.

49
00:02:28.442 --> 00:02:30.063
"You did it!"

50
00:02:30.503 --> 00:02:30.824
she said.

51
00:02:33.728 --> 00:02:35.829
"Now, where are we?"

52
00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:38.090
"I don't know.

53
00:02:38.771 --> 00:02:40.172
But at least it's dry."

54
00:02:41.092 --> 00:02:41.992
Zann looked around.

55
00:02:42.793 --> 00:02:46.395
They had landed on an open plain surrounded by a dark forest.

56
00:02:47.655 --> 00:02:49.356
A flash of lightning lit up the sky.

57
00:02:50.377 --> 00:02:55.360
Strange lights flickered on and off, and strange sounds came from every direction.

58
00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.861
The air crackled with strong magical energy.

59
00:02:58.881 --> 00:03:01.063
"Where are we?"

60
00:03:01.403 --> 00:03:02.303
Perda asked again.

61
00:03:02.924 --> 00:03:05.037
This time she sounded a little nervous.

62
00:03:06.257 --> 00:03:08.859
Zann climbed to his feet and then helped Perda up.

63
00:03:09.759 --> 00:03:11.921
She undid the Shackle spell to release his arm.

64
00:03:11.941 --> 00:03:14.362
"Come on," said Zann.

65
00:03:14.382 --> 00:03:16.423
"Let's—" "Look out!"

66
00:03:16.903 --> 00:03:20.265
Perda shouted, yanking him back as the ground opened up at their feet.

67
00:03:21.646 --> 00:03:27.529
They jumped backward as the opening grew bigger, emitting a blast of energy that sizzled several nearby trees

68
00:03:27.589 --> 00:03:28.870
into burnt stumps.

69
00:03:29.911 --> 00:03:32.212
A second later the ground closed again.

70
00:03:33.188 --> 00:03:37.371
"Let's get away from here," Perda said, backing away toward a cluster of trees.

71
00:03:37.391 --> 00:03:40.013
"Stop!" Zann cried.

72
00:03:40.874 --> 00:03:45.777
One of the trees was reaching toward Perda, its branches snaking out like tentacles.

73
00:03:46.738 --> 00:03:50.020
Zann grabbed her and dragged her out of range just in time.

74
00:03:50.881 --> 00:03:55.044
He didn't stop until they were in the open, well away from any of the trees.

75
00:03:55.064 --> 00:03:57.766
"What's wrong with this world?"

76
00:03:58.086 --> 00:04:00.488
Perda said, looking worried and confused.

77
00:04:01.812 --> 00:04:03.233
Zann didn't answer for a second.

78
00:04:04.053 --> 00:04:07.475
He was staring at something passing by on the far side of the plain.

79
00:04:08.436 --> 00:04:10.277
Something huge and hairy.

80
00:04:11.097 --> 00:04:18.561
It looked like a giant spider, but with ten legs and three long, curved teeth sticking out from

81
00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:19.022
its mouth.

82
00:04:19.042 --> 00:04:21.883
"I think I just figured it out."

83
00:04:22.864 --> 00:04:26.206
He pointed at the creature, which was too far away to notice them.

84
00:04:26.226 --> 00:04:27.987
"See that?

85
00:04:28.547 --> 00:04:31.028
I think it's a deca-stinger.

86
00:04:31.048 --> 00:04:36.130
I recognize it from one of my parents' books— Creatures of the Known Magical Worlds."

87
00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.371
"S—so this is a known magical world?"

88
00:04:40.771 --> 00:04:41.391
Perda asked.

89
00:04:41.411 --> 00:04:42.571
"Which one?"

90
00:04:43.512 --> 00:04:44.432
Zann gulped.

91
00:04:44.452 --> 00:04:47.153
"I think it's Fardark."

92
00:04:47.173 --> 00:04:49.973
"Fardark?" Perda echoed.

93
00:04:49.993 --> 00:04:51.474
"Oh boy."

94
00:04:52.754 --> 00:04:54.575
Zann knew exactly how she felt.

95
00:04:55.555 --> 00:04:59.436
Fardark was known for its dark magic and dangerous creatures.

96
00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:05.982
Zann tried to remember what else he'd read about Fardark, but he was soon interrupted.

97
00:05:06.002 --> 00:05:07.322
"Look out!"

98
00:05:07.562 --> 00:05:08.862
Perda cried, pointing up.

99
00:05:09.703 --> 00:05:10.663
Zann glanced up.

100
00:05:11.543 --> 00:05:15.164
A huge dragon was flying down toward them, its claws bared.

101
00:05:16.004 --> 00:05:22.626
Boiling droplets fell from its mouth like hail, leaving burned spots sizzling all around Zann and Perda.

102
00:05:23.827 --> 00:05:28.468
Zann raised his hand to throw up a Shield spell, but realized it was no use.

103
00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.962
Once again the vortex had drained most of their energy.

104
00:05:33.783 --> 00:05:36.204
Their magic might not be strong enough to protect them.

105
00:05:37.165 --> 00:05:38.445
"Run!" Zann yelled.

106
00:05:39.046 --> 00:05:41.788
He grabbed Perda's hand and sprinted across the plain.

107
00:05:42.668 --> 00:05:44.809
The dragon turned and came at them again.

108
00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:51.253
This time Zann heard Perda cry out as one of the droplets burned her arm, leaving a red

109
00:05:51.353 --> 00:05:53.435
mark. "This way!"

110
00:05:53.935 --> 00:05:55.436
Zann pulled her toward the trees.

111
00:05:56.248 --> 00:06:00.252
They would just have to hope they weren't the same kind of trees that had tried to grab

112
00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:05.296
them. As lightning flashed again, he spotted a hollow tree trunk just ahead.

113
00:06:06.177 --> 00:06:08.359
Pulling Perda with him, he ducked into it.

114
00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.342
A rain of sizzling droplets burned the earth around them.

115
00:06:12.362 --> 00:06:15.465
"Did that dragon see us hide in here?"

116
00:06:16.025 --> 00:06:17.407
Perda whispered, peering out.

117
00:06:17.427 --> 00:06:19.208
"I don't know."

118
00:06:19.829 --> 00:06:20.789
Zann looked out too.

119
00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:28.504
The dragon landed with a thud, its red eyes searching the darkness and its nostrils sniffing the air.

120
00:06:29.365 --> 00:06:30.766
Suddenly there was a wail.

121
00:06:31.527 --> 00:06:36.051
A second later the deca-stinger appeared and flung itself onto the dragon!

122
00:06:37.032 --> 00:06:41.856
The two huge beasts rolled in the dirt, clawing each other and howling.

123
00:06:41.876 --> 00:06:44.058
"This could be our chance!"

124
00:06:44.379 --> 00:06:44.979
Zann whispered.

125
00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.182
"Let's get out of here while they're both distracted."
